# Resume and cover-letter format

**Render:** markdown → HTML (`resume-corporate.css` / `cover-letter-corporate.css`) → one-page PDF. Fill remaining bottom whitespace with complete bullets and transcript-backed education lines. Keep `md/`, `html/`, and `pdf/` in sync.

**Resume header:** name and contact only. Do **not** put a target job title under the name. Cover letters may keep the target title.

**Layout:** follow `Resumes & Cover Letters/Examples/` (Ethan Ruiz PDFs) for structure and type only — never copy their content. Contact line is phone | email | NY / NJ | LinkedIn. Base is New York / New Jersey. Section titles: **Relevant Experience**, **Projects**, **Education**, **Skills/Interests**. Company left / location right; italic role left / dates right; disc bullets. Skills/Interests uses `Skills:`, `Interests:`, `Community:` labels like the examples.

**Summary:** a **full three-line** justified paragraph (three sentences that wrap to three complete lines). First person, spoken tone — write like a person, not a keyword list. Affirmative. Not a one-liner. Not a short last line.

**Write only what he has done.** Never list tools, products, titles, or methods he has not used. Rephrase product constraints as positive facts.

**Every bullet is a full, robust sentence** (subject implied or stated, complete predicate, ending period). No fragment lists.

**Section order:** header → summary → **Relevant Experience** → **Projects** → **Education** → **Skills/Interests**.

**Experience:** only employers from [`Career/Experience/Jobs`](Career/Experience/Jobs) (currently **BariAccess**). Current role first. Do **not** list a Projects-folder product as an employer. TREI and ABA may appear in BariAccess bullets only — do **not** put ABA in Skills/Interests. Do not write `(one of two primary engineers)` in the role line — put it in a bullet.

City of Elizabeth (intern) is employment, not a product packet; keep it after BariAccess until it has its own Jobs folder.

**Projects:** only packets from [`Career/Experience/Projects`](Career/Experience/Projects). Format each like Relevant Experience: **name | location**, italic role | dates, then disc bullets. Stack goes in bullets, not in the location slot.

**LaunchPage Studio is one Project.** List products **inside** that block. Do **not** give Automotive Operations System or TaxTracker Pro their own Projects entries. Product name is **Automotive Operations System** (never Alex Road Service). Product name is **TaxTracker Pro** (not TaxTacker, not TaxTracker). Do **not** put TREI here — TREI is the BariAccess job product.

